EXT. HARBOUR WALL - LOW TIDE - DUSK

Wind. Gulls. CALLUM (20s) sits on the wall with his boots over the drop. His brother FINN (late 20s) climbs up beside him without a word.

FINN
Mum thinks you are at work.

CALLUM
Mum thinks a lot of things.

A long silence. The tide is out. Boats sit on the mud at angles.

CALLUM (CONT'D)
Dad said Granddad's suicide was a beautiful sacrifice. Said it like it was the bravest thing he ever saw.

FINN
Dad says things when he is drunk.

CALLUM
Maybe he was right.

Finn does not answer. He does not leave either.

INT. FINN'S FLAT - NIGHT

Callum on the sofa under a blanket. Finn in the kitchen doorway with two mugs.

FINN
I do not know what to say. So I am going to say the thing on the poster at work.

CALLUM
Go on then.

FINN
Samaritans. 116 123. Free, any time. I will ring it with you or I will sit here while you do. Your call.

Callum almost laughs.

CALLUM
That is the poster?

FINN
That is the poster.

Callum takes the mug.

END CARD: If you are struggling, you can call Samaritans free on 116 123 at any time, or visit samaritans.org.
